    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bennett Springs sprang up in the late 19th century as a ranching outpost drawn by its natural springs amid Nevada's mining boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bennett_springs_nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Its geothermal spring pours 10 gallons per minute at 88°F, creating a rare oasis amid the Great Basin desert.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bennett_springs_nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bennett Springs sits at 5,272 feet on the western slopes of Meadow Valley, 7 miles north of Caliente.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bennett_springs_nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Droughts threaten Bennett Springs' riparian habitat by shrinking spring flow, stressing local cottonwoods and wildlife.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bennett_springs_nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The springs emerge from fault‑conduits in volcanic formations, a hallmark of the Basin and Range province.",
